    "rationale": "HPS type 2 results from deficiency of the AP-3 complex β3A subunit encoded by AP3B1. Defective trafficking to lysosome-related organelles affects melanosomes, platelet dense granules, and immune-cell granules, producing albinism, bleeding, neutropenia, and immune dysfunction. Strongest alternative resolved: Chediak-Higashi syndrome also causes albinism, infection and bleeding, but it characteristically produces giant lysosomal granules in leukocytes. Their absence together with neutropenia and absent platelet dense granules supports AP3B1-associated Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome type 2."
